<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Terra Luz feels like a warm, sun-washed escape: colorful, relaxed, and full of character. The design pulls from the textures and colors of Old Havana and Mexico City, layering foundational desert terrain neutrals of Sunbaked Terracotta, Sage Cactus and warm whites \(like Warm Sand\) with bold moments of cobalt Kahlo Blue and Desert Marigold, a golden yellow, in a way that feels collected and lived-in, not overly styled.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
